PowOS web: i32 ops whose results depended on the undefined upper 32 bits of i32 values in the Wasm backend
(which computes i32 ops with 64-bit arithmetic):
- add2_i32/sub2_i32: carry/borrow from a 64-bit add/sub never saw bit 32, so AArch64 ADDS/CMN on W registers set
  C wrongly and conditional branches went the wrong way. This crashed systemd under qemu-wasm (found with
  targets/web/test/probe: interpreting only libsystemd-shared's hashmap code fixed it).
- mulu2/muls2/muluh/mulsh_i32: operands not zero/sign-extended before the 64-bit multiply; mulsh shifted unsigned.
- clz32/ctz32: zero test on the whole 64-bit register.
- extract_i32/sextract_i32: 32-bit shift amounts used with 64-bit shifts (wrong bits extracted).
- bswap16/bswap32: TCG_BSWAP_OS (sign-extended output) ignored.

